    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello!\r\n\r\n> How do I correctly import and use luarocks packages with mini.deps?\r\n\r\nCurrently there is no support for Luarocks through 'mini.deps' directly, I am afraid. it is only limited to plugins organized as Git repos.\r\n\r\nIf the 'luarocks.nvim' works for you, then use it. It probably needs to be installed/added (`MiniDeps.add('vhyrro/luarocks.nvim')`) before any Luarocks package installation.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello!</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How do I correctly import and use luarocks packages with mini.deps?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Currently there is no support for Luarocks through 'mini.deps' directly, I am afraid. it is only limited to plugins organized as Git repos.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If the 'luarocks.nvim' works for you, then use it. It probably needs to be installed/added (<code class=\"notranslate\">MiniDeps.add('vhyrro/luarocks.nvim')</code>) before any Luarocks package installation.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hello!\n\nHow do I correctly import and use luarocks packages with mini.deps?\n\nCurrently there is no support for Luarocks through 'mini.deps' directly, I am afraid. it is only limited to plugins organized as Git repos.\nIf the 'luarocks.nvim' works for you, then use it. It probably needs to be installed/added (MiniDeps.add('vhyrro/luarocks.nvim')) before any Luarocks package installation.",
